\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What is and is not gained by deriving the complex mass field. An assigned complex mass is the correct one-particle baseline: the new content is the field's geometric provenance, determinant relation, and exact collinearity zero locus, not the existence of phase physics by itself. None of the three models predicts the absolute mass scale, and all retain regulator-dependent ultraviolet structure.}}{5}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
